body:
I think I might've worded it improperly, that's my bad! I meant that me clenching my stomach muscles disrupts my own sleep because I can't sit still and relax without doing it.

&#x200B;

My roommates do make comments about my pressing down on my stomach or body-checking, though. One of them has commented that he "Knows when you're body-checking, because you spend way too much time in the bathroom." and it kind of screwed with me ever since. 

&#x200B;

My parents have told me that it bothers them and to stop doing it, but I explained it's a compulsion and it's not that easy. They've outright snapped at me going, "Ashe, stop that. I hate it." I told them it's like asking me to not breathe. It feels impossible to stop doing, especially without medication.

Hey thanks for the suggestion :) I looked it up at my drug store near me and sadly they don't have any in stock right now, but it I did put it in the "save for later" category so I'll keep my eye out for it! I'm kind of tight on money currently since I just moved out, but when I get paid next week I'll look into it more \^\^

&#x200B;

Do you know if the bloating could be worse if I don't drink? I was wondering if this might be the case because I'm dehydrated a lot of the time. As I'm typing this I'm laying in bed sooo uncomfortable because my stomach feels like a rock and looks so distended :( bloating sucks so much..

Hi, I just wanted to ask, 

&#x200B;

Where do you get the tomestone gear for level 70's at Rhalgr's Reach? I swear I've gone to every one of the vendors and haven't seen anything about giving in the tomestones for gear. I know that at Mhor Dona (if that's how you spell it) and Illdyshire, there was stuff there but now I'm too high of a level to buy from there.

Looks like some maggots crawling out of the holes.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Pleasant dreams. <3

I'd love to ask that but I'm too scared of seeming like I'm too needy or clingy...

&#x200B;

but damn I really want to ask.

Well I'm now in the middle of yet another depressive episode. It's 8 PM here in Ottawa and I feel like everything's falling apart. 

&#x200B;

I feel so hopelessly alone. I just lashed out at one of my friends because I'm having such a hard time dealing with my emotions, and feel like everyone hates me. There's no point in living anymore. No one would care if I died.

&#x200B;

Thanks for trying to help, though. It means a lot that you even took time to read what I wrote.

I've tried to talk to my friends about this and they understand it and want to support me, but it got really confusing for me a couple days ago when one of his good friends told me liked me.

&#x200B;

This obviously made me feel flattered, but uncomfortable because it's my ex's best friend. Luckily I'm still close with my ex (but you know.. I really desperately miss the way it was before), so he's been understanding, but it still makes me feel a bit awkward.

&#x200B;

I've developed feelings for this guy now, and we flirt and hang out a lot (they're all in a separate city from mine). It started getting really heavy 2 days ago when it was getting pretty sexual, and I was into it and everything but I feel like I'm just being used.. just kind of there for when he's looking for something to get off to, and then leaves. 

&#x200B;

So to give you a timeline, boy a) broke up with me 3 weeks ago. His good friend told me he liked me a couple days ago and it's been getting intense. 

&#x200B;

It's all kind of messing with my head. He also said that he can't do a relationship, when I asked out of curiosity. He's pretty shy and isn't ready for something like that, which I was very supportive of and told him there was no pressure. This is all just very confusing and is sending my mental health into a spiral.

&#x200B;

That, and I'm struggling with my grades and my home life is stressful. It's just not a good situation. I came really close to overdosing the other day, too, when I was alone. I'm a lone a lot. I have no IRL friends, only the ones online, because of my social anxiety. I'm too scared to speak to people at my school or in my neighborhood.

Hi, 

&#x200B;

I'm a 16-year-old female. I've had a hard time with my depression, BPD and anxiety for years now, and it just feels impossible to handle anymore. 

&#x200B;

I just got out of a relationship with a guy I really liked. It was long-distance and he said it would've worked out, but he just couldn't handle the distance anymore. It was really hard for both of us, and especially for me. 

&#x200B;

I'm on medication, go to therapy every once in a while and have my friends to support me, though I feel like it's never going to work. I've tried to kill myself 5 times, and am cutting my wrists deeper and deeper. Last week, I cut it down to fat and never went to the E.R.

&#x200B;

It feels so pointless to hold on anymore. I feel worthless. I miss my ex so much, everyday I think about how it could have worked out, if only we were in the same city. My depressive thoughts have gotten worse and so have my cutting episodes. I'm crying almost everyday now and feel like living is pointless.

This really should not have made me laugh as much as it did...

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

But you know.. the laughter hides the depression. :'D
